# Call System Protection — SACRED INFRASTRUCTURE

The call system is **core business infrastructure**. Treat every change as high-risk unless explicitly scoped to UI-only with zero logic diff.

## DO NOT BREAK

- `startCrmOutboundCall` and outbound call initiation pipeline
- `OutboundSystemHandoffPage` (`outbound_system_handoff_page.dart`)
- Post-call capture flow (`PostCallCaptureStrip`, `PostCallWizardScreen`, `post_call_wizard.dart`)
- Return prompt (`CallReturnPromptHost`)
- Callback queue and CRM call drafts / draft recovery
- Confidence badges and call memory hints
- Manager/customer call strips (`customer_crm_call_strip`, command center chrome)
- Consultant call workflows (`consultant_calls_page.dart`, `call_screen.dart`)
- Device call log sync semantics (honest platform limits on iOS)
- Post-call AI enrichment wiring (providers/services — not cosmetic-only)

## UI changes in call screens

Allowed **only** when:

- Providers, repositories, Firestore paths, and navigation contracts are **unchanged**
- Call state machine, handoff, and post-call wizard steps are **unchanged**
- No new listeners, timers, or duplicate fetches introduced
- All CTAs remain wired (dial, handoff, post-call, return, history)

## Forbidden without explicit user approval

- Refactoring call initiation or post-call state machines
- Changing route paths for `/call`, `/call/summary`, `/consultant/calls`
- Modifying `startCrmOutboundCall` signature or side effects
- Removing recovery/draft/return prompt behavior
- Faking call log capabilities on unsupported platforms

## Required verification after any call-area touch

```bash
flutter analyze
flutter test
```

Manual QA: start call → active call UI → end call → post-call wizard → draft recovery → return prompt → calls list refresh.

## Related protected files (non-exhaustive)

- `lib/features/calls/**`
- `lib/features/crm_customers/presentation/widgets/customer_crm_call_strip.dart`
- `lib/widgets/premium/premium_call_center_chrome.dart`
- `lib/features/manager_command_center/**` (call center views)

If UI rebuild touches these files, state **preserved call flows** explicitly in the delivery summary.
